psplash_fb_text_size: a text has one line more than it has newlines

The height was the number of newlines times the font height (one line when
there are none), so a message of n lines was placed as if it had n - 1:
psplash_draw_msg puts the text's bottom at the split line, and the last line
went below it, into the rows of the progress bar, which then painted over it.
The clear rectangle missed that line as well. openccu-lite's end-of-boot
message has four lines, and its web address was half covered by the bar.

--- psplash.orig/psplash-fb.c	2025-05-13 13:08:00.000000000 +0200
+++ psplash/psplash-fb.c	2026-09-13 09:40:36.757113803 +0200
@@ -568,7 +568,8 @@
     }

   *width  = (w > mw) ? w : mw;
-  *height = (h == 0) ? font->height : h;
+  /* every text has one line more than it has newlines */
+  *height = h + font->height;
 }

 void
